{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1150756-convention-books-word-counts","id":1150756,"title":"Convention Books word counts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-18T13:32:31-07:00","id":1150756,"title":"Convention Books word counts","content":"Haven't you thought Convention Books word counts are generally lower (perhaps 60~70%) than the Tradition and Clan Books? Or is that just my personal feeling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T17:11:57-07:00","id":1150834,"title":"","content":"What more would you have them say?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T18:46:12-07:00","id":1150864,"title":"","content":"Do you mean the revised edition Convention Book: Iteration X and it's post-Time of Judgment followups or the first and second edition Technocracy: [Convention Name Here] sourcebooks? Because the Technocracy: Name ones were the same size as most of the original 1st/2nd ed splatbooks from all the lines, while ItXRev was the same size as the revised Tradition books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T21:45:18-07:00","id":1150893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1150756-convention-books-word-counts?p=1150864#post1150864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean the revised edition Convention Book: Iteration X and it's post-Time of Judgment followups or the first and second edition Technocracy: [Convention Name Here] sourcebooks? Because the Technocracy: Name ones were the same size as most of the original 1st/2nd ed splatbooks from all the lines, while ItXRev was the same size as the revised Tradition books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Post-revised Convention splatbooks, after ItXRev.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T02:55:55-07:00","id":1152443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1150756-convention-books-word-counts#post1150756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haven't you thought Convention Books word counts are generally lower (perhaps 60~70%) than the Tradition and Clan Books? Or is that just my personal feeling?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they seem to be so. Perhaps because the chapters about Technocracy's history are repeating the same information that is written in all the Convention Books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T03:05:29-07:00","id":1152739,"title":"","content":"No.<br /> <br /> Using revised editions and a page count that includes the front and back covers as pages (as I am using the PDFs).<br /> <br /> Order of Hermes - 106<br /> Syndicate - 106<br /> Void Engineers - 112<br /> Clanbook Tremere - 106<br /> Akashic Brotherhood - 106<br /> <br /> Hope that helps <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11780\" data-vbnamecard=\"11780\">Posthumanity</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T06:57:22-07:00","id":1152791,"title":"","content":"Word count isn't going to be the same as page count, as depending on things like text size, font style, and how much margin there is per page, one page may have as much as 50% to 100% more words than another. (If you have the revised edition Werewolf tribe books, at least two of the pre made character templates in Fianna have about 200 more words in them than the others, and had to be printed with a smaller type than usual to compensate.) Back in the late 90s, there were a couple of game companies kind of infamous for combining a somewhat larger type face with really wide page margins to put out books that had around 100 pages, but only about as much written material as would've covered about 50 pages in your average White Wolf, TSR/WotC or other company title.<br /> <br /> I've not seen any of the post-White Wolf Convention book PDFs, so I couldn't say what their word counts might've been compared to the earlier revised hardcopy books. It's entirely possible that the word counts are lower, but without seeing the development outline given to the writers, it's kind of hard to say for sure. (Those would always have each chapter or even subsection of a book broken down into how many words it should have; I think in revised era, book chapters usually averaged about 20K words each, but this would sometimes fluctuate - the history section in Guide to the Traditions weighed in at about 40K I think.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 10-26-2017, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T18:03:14-07:00","id":1155605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1150756-convention-books-word-counts?p=1152791#post1152791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Word count isn't going to be the same as page count, as depending on things like text size, font style, and how much margin there is per page, one page may have as much as 50% to 100% more words than another. (If you have the revised edition Werewolf tribe books, at least two of the pre made character templates in Fianna have about 200 more words in them than the others, and had to be printed with a smaller type than usual to compensate.) Back in the late 90s, there were a couple of game companies kind of infamous for combining a somewhat larger type face with really wide page margins to put out books that had around 100 pages, but only about as much written material as would've covered about 50 pages in your average White Wolf, TSR/WotC or other company title.<br /> <br /> I've not seen any of the post-White Wolf Convention book PDFs, so I couldn't say what their word counts might've been compared to the earlier revised hardcopy books. It's entirely possible that the word counts are lower, but without seeing the development outline given to the writers, it's kind of hard to say for sure. (Those would always have each chapter or even subsection of a book broken down into how many words it should have; I think in revised era, book chapters usually averaged about 20K words each, but this would sometimes fluctuate - the history section in Guide to the Traditions weighed in at about 40K I think.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya you\u2019re right, i totally misread the topic and thought \u2018page count\u2019 instead. Silly me.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s only one way to check! Go in there and start counting words per page. Maybe do a comparison of five different pages (without art) from 5 different books and see what you come up with. I bet it\u2019d only take you an hour or so and that people would be interested to see what you came up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T00:50:04-07:00","id":1155663,"title":"","content":"Running a copy-paste into a text document, the Revised Tradbooks come in at 60-75k words, while the Convention books come in about 50-55k words, so that's about 25% between the shortest Convention book and the longest Tradition book and about 8-9% between longest Convention book and shortest Tradbook..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T02:12:54-07:00","id":1155673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1150756-convention-books-word-counts?p=1155663#post1155663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Running a copy-paste into a text document, the Revised Tradbooks come in at 60-75k words, while the Convention books come in about 50-55k words, so that's about 25% between the shortest Convention book and the longest Tradition book and about 8-9% between longest Convention book and shortest Tradbook..</div> </div> </div> </div>I have always thought Convention books are generally 20% shorter than its Tradition cousins. Your validation is much appreciated. Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}